+    notes: V1 had no WebAuthn package; interactive PIN retry for FIDO2 operations went through the global, cross-applet Fido2Session.KeyCollector. V2 introduces Yubico.YubiKit.WebAuthn, a new higher-level package built on Yubico.YubiKit.Ctap2 (ICtap2Session); its WebAuthnClient accepts an optional Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Credentials.ICredentialPrompt (set via WebAuthnClientOptions.CredentialPrompt - see `webauthn-client-construction-and-streams` for the options-record construction change), an async, cancellable, context-carrying callback (CredentialPromptContext, carrying Kind, Scope, RetriesRemaining, and IsRetry) invoked when an operation needs a PIN and the caller did not pass pinBytes directly. The client, not the prompt, owns the bounded retry loop (WebAuthnClientOptions.MaxPromptAttempts, default 3, now caller-configurable); returning null from the prompt means the user declined, not a retry request. This replaces the credential-collection part of KeyCollector only for WebAuthn; lower-level CTAP callers pass PIN bytes to ClientPin to acquire a token, then supply PinUvAuthParam/PinUvAuthProtocol through credential options on ICtap2Session (omitting the mutually exclusive uv key). Touch is separate; supply IUserPresencePrompt through CTAP2 SessionCreationOptions. HID reports DeviceWaiting on a user-presence-needed keep-alive; SmartCard ordinary creation/assertion reports PolicyRequires before the APDU, while generic helper traffic has no modeled notification. A notification is not proof of gesture, UV or RP acceptance. Review the credential prompt's exactly-sized-buffer and ownership-transfer contract against any existing v1 KeyCollector implementation being carried forward.
